        <mxCell id="AMVr_15TMgkF3U7xx4dS-5" value="&lt;p data-end=&quot;134&quot; data-start=&quot;0&quot;&gt;ТЕМПЕРАТУРА НА РІЗОНІНГ МОДЕЛЯХ (Я ДУМАЮ ЗДЕБІЛЬШОГО) НЕ МІНЯЄТЬСЯ!!!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Here are suggested temperature settings for each agent, along with the rationale for why those values best fit their respective roles:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr data-end=&quot;139&quot; data-start=&quot;136&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3 data-end=&quot;163&quot; data-start=&quot;141&quot;&gt;1. &lt;code data-end=&quot;163&quot; data-start=&quot;148&quot;&gt;planner_agent&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul data-end=&quot;205&quot; data-start=&quot;164&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;205&quot; data-start=&quot;164&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;205&quot; data-start=&quot;166&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;205&quot; data-start=&quot;166&quot;&gt;Suggested &lt;code data-end=&quot;198&quot; data-start=&quot;178&quot;&gt;temperature_to_use&lt;/code&gt;: 0.5&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;528&quot; data-start=&quot;207&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;221&quot; data-start=&quot;207&quot;&gt;Rationale:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br data-end=&quot;224&quot; data-start=&quot;221&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The planner’s job is to outline a complex research report—generating section titles, key questions, a report title, and a bit of background context. You want enough randomness to surface creative yet coherent ways of structuring a report. A mid-range temperature (around 0.5) strikes the balance between:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul data-end=&quot;755&quot; data-start=&quot;529&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;643&quot; data-start=&quot;529&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;643&quot; data-start=&quot;531&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;546&quot; data-start=&quot;531&quot;&gt;Creativity:&lt;/strong&gt; Allows the model to propose novel section headings or unexpected angles that still make sense.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;755&quot; data-start=&quot;644&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;755&quot; data-start=&quot;646&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;660&quot; data-start=&quot;646&quot;&gt;Coherence:&lt;/strong&gt; Keeps the outline focused and logically organized rather than too “stream-of-consciousness.”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;1046&quot; data-start=&quot;757&quot;&gt;At 0.5, the planner can wander into less-obvious subtopics without veering completely off-course. If you set it much higher (e.g. 0.8+), the outline might be too imaginative and lose structure; much lower (e.g. 0.2) would be too rigid, often producing very formulaic, predictable outlines.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr data-end=&quot;1051&quot; data-start=&quot;1048&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3 data-end=&quot;1076&quot; data-start=&quot;1053&quot;&gt;2. &lt;code data-end=&quot;1076&quot; data-start=&quot;1060&quot;&gt;thinking_agent&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul data-end=&quot;1118&quot; data-start=&quot;1077&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;1118&quot; data-start=&quot;1077&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;1118&quot; data-start=&quot;1079&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;1118&quot; data-start=&quot;1079&quot;&gt;Suggested &lt;code data-end=&quot;1111&quot; data-start=&quot;1091&quot;&gt;temperature_to_use&lt;/code&gt;: 0.3&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;1509&quot; data-start=&quot;1120&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;1134&quot; data-start=&quot;1120&quot;&gt;Rationale:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br data-end=&quot;1137&quot; data-start=&quot;1134&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The thinking agent’s role is to reflect on previous iterations—“What have we learned? What new areas to explore? Were we successful?”—essentially surmising and critically evaluating the research progress. You want the output to be concise, logically precise, and grounded in what’s already happened rather than freewheeling creativity. A lower temperature (≈ 0.3) ensures:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul data-end=&quot;1827&quot; data-start=&quot;1510&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;1653&quot; data-start=&quot;1510&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;1653&quot; data-start=&quot;1512&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;1538&quot; data-start=&quot;1512&quot;&gt;Determinism &amp;amp; Clarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Thoughts stay focused on the salient points from prior iterations, producing consistent, actionable reflections.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;1827&quot; data-start=&quot;1654&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;1827&quot; data-start=&quot;1656&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;1683&quot; data-start=&quot;1656&quot;&gt;Sufficient Flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; 0.3 still allows minor variation in phrasing and nuance, so it won’t be so repetitive that every iteration’s reflection reads exactly the same.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;2127&quot; data-start=&quot;1829&quot;&gt;If the temperature were set to 0.0, you’d likely get overly “robotic” responses that can’t incorporate any subtle nuance. Anything above 0.5 could introduce fluff or diverge into tangential ideas, which isn’t ideal for a module that’s supposed to introspect on specific observations and next steps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr data-end=&quot;2132&quot; data-start=&quot;2129&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3 data-end=&quot;2162&quot; data-start=&quot;2134&quot;&gt;3. &lt;code data-end=&quot;2162&quot; data-start=&quot;2141&quot;&gt;knowledge_gap_agent&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul data-end=&quot;2204&quot; data-start=&quot;2163&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;2204&quot; data-start=&quot;2163&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;2204&quot; data-start=&quot;2165&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;2204&quot; data-start=&quot;2165&quot;&gt;Suggested &lt;code data-end=&quot;2197&quot; data-start=&quot;2177&quot;&gt;temperature_to_use&lt;/code&gt;: 0.2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;2536&quot; data-start=&quot;2206&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;2220&quot; data-start=&quot;2206&quot;&gt;Rationale:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br data-end=&quot;2223&quot; data-start=&quot;2220&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;This agent must critically analyze “findings and thoughts” to identify very specific gaps in knowledge and decide if the research is complete. Its main job is precision: flagging exactly “what’s missing?” If you want reliable, repeatable identification of gaps, a very low temperature (around 0.2) is recommended:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul data-end=&quot;2820&quot; data-start=&quot;2537&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;2646&quot; data-start=&quot;2537&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;2646&quot; data-start=&quot;2539&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;2558&quot; data-start=&quot;2539&quot;&gt;High Precision:&lt;/strong&gt; At 0.2, the model is strongly guided toward the most obvious, least speculative gaps.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;2820&quot; data-start=&quot;2647&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;2820&quot; data-start=&quot;2649&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;2675&quot; data-start=&quot;2649&quot;&gt;Minimal Hallucination:&lt;/strong&gt; Lower randomness ensures the identified gaps really match the history of findings, rather than inventing tangential “gaps” that aren’t relevant.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;3088&quot; data-start=&quot;2822&quot;&gt;Going all the way to 0.0 could make the agent somewhat inflexible—if it sees a pattern it might never deviate from it. At 0.2, it still has a tiny bit of allowance to phrase things in a slightly fresh way, but remains extremely consistent about what to call a “gap.”&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr data-end=&quot;3093&quot; data-start=&quot;3090&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h3 data-end=&quot;3123&quot; data-start=&quot;3095&quot;&gt;4. &lt;code data-end=&quot;3123&quot; data-start=&quot;3102&quot;&gt;tool_selector_agent&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul data-end=&quot;3165&quot; data-start=&quot;3124&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;3165&quot; data-start=&quot;3124&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;3165&quot; data-start=&quot;3126&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;3165&quot; data-start=&quot;3126&quot;&gt;Suggested &lt;code data-end=&quot;3158&quot; data-start=&quot;3138&quot;&gt;temperature_to_use&lt;/code&gt;: 0.1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;3456&quot; data-start=&quot;3167&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;3181&quot; data-start=&quot;3167&quot;&gt;Rationale:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br data-end=&quot;3184&quot; data-start=&quot;3181&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;The tool selector’s task is to map each knowledge gap to the most appropriate specialized agent(s) and propose very concise (3–6 word) queries. This demands near-deterministic precision—almost no creative reinterpretation of the gap. A temperature of 0.1 keeps the output:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul data-end=&quot;3666&quot; data-start=&quot;3457&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;3565&quot; data-start=&quot;3457&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;3565&quot; data-start=&quot;3459&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;3484&quot; data-start=&quot;3459&quot;&gt;Highly Deterministic:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensures the model consistently chooses the same agent mapping for a given gap.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;li data-end=&quot;3666&quot; data-start=&quot;3566&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;3666&quot; data-start=&quot;3568&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-end=&quot;3580&quot; data-start=&quot;3568&quot;&gt;Concise:&lt;/strong&gt; Reduces the chance of needless variation in how it phrases the “agent query” strings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-end=&quot;4089&quot; data-start=&quot;3668&quot;&gt;If you set temperature to 0.0, you risk having absolutely no flexibility (edge-case: it might repeat identical phrasing each time, which could be okay but sometimes prevents slight rewording to match a new context). At 0.1, there’s just enough leeway to re-order keywords or tweak phrasing without altering intent. Pushing above 0.2 could introduce unwanted creative mixing of agent roles or overly verbose query strings.&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-890" y="2230" width="2190" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AMVr_15TMgkF3U7xx4dS-6" value="Ще говорив, що я б додав обмеженян по часу на кожного агента" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-220" y="740" width="60" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AMVr_15TMgkF3U7xx4dS-8" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="780" y="710" width="1200" height="545" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AMVr_15TMgkF3U7xx4dS-9" value="В промпті дописати як він викликаєтьяс" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1050" y="670" width="240" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AMVr_15TMgkF3U7xx4dS-11" value="Моя Реалізація Через Те, Що Я Лінивий (+ обмаль часу&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;) Підримує Лише Моделі з Structured Output&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="235" y="860" width="60" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AMVr_15TMgkF3U7xx4dS-12" value="Напевне треба робити спрощену версію через те, що мій скілл прорамування не такий класний" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-500" y="840" width="60" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
